infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title AsyncWorker: heavy work off the JS thread
  desc Three phases, two thread hops — the slow part runs where it can't freeze the event loop
  sequences
    - label Marshal inputs to plain C/C++ data
      desc Main JS thread, before Execute. Copy each napi_value into raw data (a std::vector) usable off-thread.
    - label Execute(): heavy CPU work off-thread
      desc libuv thread-pool thread, so the event loop keeps serving. Touch NO napi_value here — the engine isn't yours on this thread.
    - label OnOK() / OnError(): marshal and deliver
      desc Back on the main JS thread. Convert raw output to JS values and invoke the callback with result or error.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e #14b8a6
